 the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 206 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 54.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.1 to 4.6. December accounts for 6% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 101 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,842.73 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or genuine needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts [1] and [2] to confirm they align with the body's stated needs. Review the distribution of contracts across awardees to ensure no single provider is overrepresented. Verify if multiple contracts served the same purpose to assess potential duplication.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["h6sF92iicKZ%2FR5QFTlaM4A%3D%3D","OBEgDdvY0JNWhbmkna2nXQ%3D%3D","LCfZU1p6w8ykU02jNGj1Fw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}